git checkout -q -B dev origin/dev && mkdir -p .forgejo paper && cat > .forgejo/CODEOWNERS <<'EOF'
\.forgejo/CODEOWNERS @paper-repo
\.forgejo/document\.json @paper-repo
README\.md @paper-repo
paper/.* @paper-repo
template/.* @venue-repo
code/.* @experiment-repo
results/.* @experiment-repo
figures/.* @figtab-repo
tables/.* @figtab-repo
refs/.* @idea-repo
EOF
cat > .forgejo/document.json <<'EOF'
{"command":"cd paper && latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error main.tex","output":"paper/main.pdf"}
EOF
cat > README.md <<'EOF'
# paper-repo — the delivered paper and its release

Layout (who delivers each path is in `.forgejo/CODEOWNERS`):

| Path | Content | Delivered by |
|---|---|---|
| `paper/` | LaTeX sources of the paper (`main.tex`, sections, appendix, checklist) | report |
| `template/` | the venue's official style files and checklist template, unmodified | venue |
| `code/` | all code, environment and dependency versions, data acquisition, seeds, run commands, expected run time, reproduction README mapping every table and figure to its script | analysis |
| `results/` | result files the paper's numbers come from (large files in Git LFS) | analysis |
| `figures/`, `tables/` | the delivered figures and tables with the scripts that generate them | presentation |
| `refs/` | bibliography sources (`.bib`) | idea |

The paper builds from `paper/main.tex` (`.forgejo/document.json`); the built PDF is not committed.
EOF
cat > paper/main.tex <<'EOF'
% Scaffold only: the venue's official template replaces this preamble once `venue-repo` declares it.
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,graphicx,booktabs,natbib}
\title{Is one run enough? Decision-level reliability of single-run SHAP attributions on tabular models}
\author{Anonymous}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\begin{abstract}
(Written from the final results.)
\end{abstract}
\section{Introduction}
\section{Related work}
\section{Setting and protocol}
\section{Experimental design}
\section{Results}
\section{Discussion and limitations}
\end{document}
EOF
git add -A && git commit -qm "Delivery layout: CODEOWNERS, document build, paper scaffold" -m "Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>" && git push -q origin dev && git log --oneline | head -2

